WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.040
Conscription is mandatory for every 
Egyptian male who has turned 18 years old 

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.880
The period of conscription is 3 years

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.000
This period is reduced to one year only 
for university and higher institute graduates

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.360
and to two years for medium institute graduates

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.480
Draft evasion is punishable 
by imprisonment, fine or both 

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.680
Military parade marches on the army hymn
The Soldiers

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.800
Military parade marches on the army hymn
Egyptian conscription tales

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.960
written by the poet Farouk Jweideh 

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.760
and composed by the musician Kamal Tawil

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.280
On our hearts we engraved the sight of homeland 

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.280
its palms, Nile and noble people 

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:32.960
On our hearts we engraved the sight of homeland 

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.720
its palms, Nile and noble people 

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.600
We protected you, O Egypt, over the time

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:48.520
so your youth remains forever

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.400
In the same vein, Colonel General 
Sedki Sobhi, Minister of Defense

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.720
approved the recruitment of 
new soldiers in April 2016

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.400
Once you graduate from college

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.480
the first impediment to your dream
of doing something with your life

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.320
becoming an engineer, a doctor, 
a manufacturer or anything

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.320
is conscription

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:24.360
It is compulsory, it is not something 
you volunteer to do or you like

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.920
You only have to do it 
to move on with your life

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.440
You are here to witness withyour own eyes the 
high level fighting capacity of your armed forces
Egyptian President 
Abdelfatah Elsisi voice

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.560
You are here to witness with your own eyes the 
high level fighting capacity of your armed forces

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:43.160
The faces and voices of the soldiers, NCOs and officers
have been hidden and altered for their safety 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.880
you shall take pride in 
them as the shield

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:51.400
against all those who dare
thwart our nation’s security

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.120
and jeopardize the 
stability of its people

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.360
I am one of the very few who were 
really excited about serving in the army

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:08.400
I thought it would be a training session 
in military science and combat skills

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:16.920
So I used to think it was mandatory for all Egyptians

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.840
Medical examination
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.320
Any person deemed medically unfit 
is released from their obligation to serve

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.320
When you are medically examined, you meet doctors

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.440
But you have to keep in mind 
that these doctors are officers

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:39.320
You should not expect any sympathy

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:45.000
so, when they tell you to take
your clothes off you obey

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.560
You stay in your underwear 

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.240
You go from one clinic to another

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.000
you start with an exam by 
the optometrist, orthopedist, 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.880
dermatologist and then gastroenterologist

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:03.120
Many pretend they are sick

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.640
Some would go with eyeglasses 
while they have excellent 6/6 vision 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.920
I saw some people faking sickness and being relieved

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.960
and some who were really sick and forced to serve 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:24.280
I do not know how to say this… I am sorry… 
this might sound strange… but they ask you to bend 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.280
Yes, the want to make sure you are a man 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:39.200
They ask you to take everything off to 
make sure you are straight and not gay

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.640
They examine you directly

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.920
The doctor examines you to see 
whether you are straight or not

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:51.560
So this doctor probably 
examines 500 butts a day

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.280
I do not remember if I took my clothes off

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.720
I guess I did

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.280
I did

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.760
but it was fast

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.480
he was looking at me from a distance 

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:17.840
he was wearing a white coat… 
so I guess he was a doctor

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.840
but yeah, I took my clothes off 

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.040
Thankfully I was deemed medically fit

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:27.720
they told me to come in two days 

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.360
At the end of it, an officer came out 
and spoke about the benefits of the army

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:37.320
how we will be fed well 
and have a good stay

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.560
He concluded by welcoming us in the armed forces

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.880
Welcome to the Armed Forces  

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:49.920
Training Center

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:54.200
Soldiers are trained in the warfare center 
for 45 days before joining the main force

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.680
The most important thing is 
to be as efficient as possible

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:05.840
If you manage to do that 
and ensure a high level of training

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:14.720
high level of ability, 
shooting and understanding, 

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.840
you will get the results WE decide

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.800
The main purpose of a training center 

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:29.520
is to teach you how to use a wireless radio 
transceiver and so on if you are in the Signal Corps

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:34.680
or how to operate a tank 
if you are in the Armored Corps

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.680
You are taught theory and practice

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:40.560
There is one thing that remains 
the same everywhere: shooting

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.200
This is what is supposed to happen, 
but it is not the case

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.920
We were taught how to shoot on the spot

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.200
Each one shot the gun 3 times

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.240
but without aiming

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:57.160
A Non Commissioned Officer would sit 
next to us, because that was our first time

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.320
You pull the trigger for 3 shots without aiming

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.920
They do not care if you hit your target or not

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:08.200
During my entire military service, 
I went to the shooting range 3 times

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:13.840
First time I fired 7 shots, then 10, and then 3

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.000
They do not teach you how to shoot

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:22.080
They explain shooting theoretically and 
there are huge numbers, difficult to control

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.240
It is impossible to explain shooting to 
every soldier andtake the time to teach them

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:33.960
No, they do not teach. 
They receive an order to go to the shooting range

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.760
They have to bring the shells to the commandment

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:43.280
For them it is not important you shoot. 
It is important to get bullet shells

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:47.600
If you fire 10 shots and bring back 9 shells 
you are in big trouble

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.720
The most important thing in the training is the shells

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:56.960
They won’t ask if the soldiers learned how to shoot 

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:59.640
no way… the officer would ask: 
where are the shells? 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
A Non Commissioned Officer (NCO)

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.920
One time we were training soldiers on shooting

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:08.800
they went to pick up the shells 
and there were about 20 cases missing

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.760
They spent two hours searching 
until they found them

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.040
I am the one who will be held accountable

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.200
So the most important thing 
is to find the missing shells

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:23.160
We did not practice shooting 
the way people think we did

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.400
shooting while standing up

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.560
so we only fired the gun lying down

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.640
"For your safety"

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:32.560
Recoil after discharge is hard to handle

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.880
so when they shoot while lying down 
they can handle it

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:40.720
It is difficult to shoot while standing up, 
let alone while moving
An Officer

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.000
So a soldier is not trained to do this
An Officer

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.560
End of story, they are not ready 
to shoot in a war

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.920
only in a firing range

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:44.720
Norvell De Atkine - a U.S. Army retired colonel

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.120
Count till 2

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.240
left right left

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.680
organize your steps

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.720
left right left

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.800
You are supposed to stay 
45 days in the warfare center 

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.600
then take a 10-day break 
before joining your unit

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.120
We spent 2 months and a half with no breaks

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.680
Only to do the show

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:09.680
Every day, we trained on how to march

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:11.400
because we were going to march 
in front of important people

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.800
every day! 

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.840
The most important thing 
soldiers learn in the first 45 days 

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.120
or 30 month conscribed reserve officers learn 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.600
is how to march so they march 
well in the military parade 

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.880
In a show

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:33.840
20 steps separate each 
formation from the other

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:38.720
Clockwise turn

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:47.880
Frankly, in the Reserve Academy, the main goal 
is to prepare us for the graduation ceremony

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.840
attended by the Minister 
and covered by the media

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.960
We spend 6 months in the Academy

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.960
4 of which – or even more – training for our graduation

00:10:55.960 --> 00:11:00.640
how to march, how to move 
the rifle, how to do the military show

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:06.480
how to write Egypt or 
anything else as we stand.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.400
Special Force individuals
choose certain reserve officers

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:13.960
who used to go to the gym
for example or body builders

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.800
and give them special training for these shows

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.760
They train them on jumping 
over fire pits for example

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.880
for the people watching, this is nice

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:33.440
They hear one step, see a synchronized movement

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.120
As a show, this coordination is so beautiful 

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:38.600
As a show

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:43.760
But as a fighter, it does not benefit you in anything 

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:48.560
Will I fight in a parade? 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
An Officer

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.880
Do I call on other soldiers in a war to write Egypt?

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:55.520
or to move the rifle from left to right? 

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:42.760
My sacrifice... my sacrifice

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:48.840
You are Egypt leader, and 
pioneer of its modern renaissance

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.440
We met some very good guys

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:57.800
Each was assigned to a different unit  

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:00.040
We were all sad to leave

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:03.720
you know, we were strangers 
when we met but close friends when we left 

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:09.640
Soldiers gather and they all look confused

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:15.760
they are leaving, their names are being called
A soldier singing

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:21.680
I thought about getting ready 
to join them and be one of them

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:26.280
I saw a non-commissioned officer 
and a sergeant calling: Attention!

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:31.360
After their training, The soldiers are distributed 
to different military units to continue their conscription

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:35.640
As soon as you reach the 
gate, you see a security soldier

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.200
He looks at everyone and says:

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:42.000
"people will look drunk, but they are not. 
But God’s punishment is tough"

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.440
He looks at you and he can 
see what you will go through

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.560
He asks you why you came and 
wonders if someone put a curse on you

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:52.120
In general, let it go

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:55.200
An insult does not stick and 
government whips are no disgrace

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.600
We were forced to get 
undressed,stay in our underwear

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.400
stand in line and clap on each other’s backs

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:05.840
We joined the battalion and 
were told to refer to Officer Adel

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:09.040
they did the paperwork and let us in

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:14.280
As we were standing, Officer Adel 
came out of the room in his boxers with a whip

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:17.720
He screamed: 
Everyone on the floor! everyone crawl!

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:22.000
They sprayed us with water, threw dirt on us 
while we crawled for a reason we ignored

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.840
This is the welcoming

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:30.680
They introduce you to your
new status, to who you are

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.240
You are nothing

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.040
When we joined, they made us love the place

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.640
They told us they were men 
and they would treat us like men

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.240
They said of course they would 
encounter some childish behavior

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:44.320
but they would still treat us 
like men, raise us to be men

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.560
You wake up at five and stand in line to clean

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:53.880
You clean around you. 
You remove fallen tree leaves
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:59.560
Every soldier shall have 
a cloth bag to clean around them

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:04.000
They shall pick up tree leaves 
and put them inside the bag

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:11.880
When there is sand in the field, you level it

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:14.720
After the cleaning line comes the fitness line

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:17.880
You are supposed to run and warm up

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:22.360
But I hereby acknowledge that fitness lines 
are the best thing the army has ever created

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:28.480
Work is divided, and you know that 
by work I mean daily cleaning chores 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:34.960
The soldier shall clean the walls, 
the sinks and the sewage canals with aluminum cables

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:40.600
They shall rub the floors with 
a brush and the toilet with the toilet brush 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:43.320
Some mop the floor and 
sweep it, others clean the toilets

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:48.160
some clean the sewage disposal canals

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.720
tasks that are in no way military 

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.960
Sometimes we would do unnecessary work

00:15:55.960 --> 00:16:02.160
for example today we have to 
move this stack of adobe bricks

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:07.320
We would spend 7 to 8 hours moving them

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.720
Then the next day we are asked 
to bring them back to where they were

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:14.200
You cannot say you do not do 
anything in the army, because you do! 

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.520
My days are so busy

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:18.560
We wake up early and go to bed exhausted at 10 pm

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:23.280
Therefore, we “practice nothingness”

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:26.800
You do not say you do nothing. 
This is a lie and a disgrace

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.840
You practice nothingness actively!

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:33.080
A rested soldier will tire you, 
a tired soldier will ensure you rest

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.400
If my soldier is rested, he will tire me

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:40.280
But if I bother him enough, I will be rested 

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:49.080
An officer or an NCO could learn you are a carpenter, for example

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:53.680
gives you a day off and take you to fix his house

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:59.120
In my unit, some soldiers went and 
painted the Commander’s apartment

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:03.040
All the unit wanted to go to the cafeteria

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:08.440
It belonged to the Brigade Commander. 
He had opened a cafeteria near the unit 

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:12.120
and soldiers worked there
He had a business for himself

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:16.960
He still ordered the soldiers 
to do gardening work in the unit 

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:19.080
and he would sell vegetables

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:22.720
I was sent once with the NCO to dig

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:27.280
I had never dug back home. 
Why would I dig in the army?

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.720
If I was digging a trench for the training, then fine

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:35.280
But to dig so that the Commander 
could sell vegetables and make a profit?  

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.000
I am not here to be a gardener! 

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:41.160
Some soldiers who work as drivers

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:44.120
They become drivers for their officers, 
and are used for running personal errands.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:50.680
If the officer is at home and wants to 
go to the mall or do something personal

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:51.920
the soldier drives him

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.400
Soldiers are a labor force

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:59.600
They are not physically and emotionally 
trained to fight in the battlefield

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:03.280
Since there is no war, soldiers practice something else 

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.600
The men of the Engineering Force

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:12.360
Egypt’s strong arm, implement 
large strategic and development projects 

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:17.040
Our Armed Forces have been 
the support of the civil sector

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:21.560
with superfluous financial, technical and human capacities

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:25.680
and no effect on their fighting ability

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:30.800
This project is launched through 
Captain Fighter Mohammed Ramzi Mohammed

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:37.320
Sir… Yes, sir… 
Captain Fighter Mohammed Ramzi Mohammed

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:41.720
management of large projects. 
The Engineering Force in the Armed Forces

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:47.120
Supervisor of the project to establish 
1056 housing units in Qena Governorate

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:50.400
Project for a permanent headquarters 
for the Women National Council

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.960
Swimming pools complex for 
training juniors in Manshiyat Naser Club

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:57.640
Those who work in these
towns, more precisely constructors

00:18:57.640 --> 00:18:59.640
are they from the Engineering Force?

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:03.360
or are they companies similar to
those who built the Suez Canal?

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:06.720
Purely Egyptian private companies.
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:09.560
Neither foreign companies nor armed forces work

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:12.920
When do armed forces interfere or help? 

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.760
Almost each town has a construction brigade

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:22.320
When a contractor feels there is a delay 
and the project will not be completed on time

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:26.280
they resort to this division. 
As you have seen, this building was erected from scratch

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:29.080
Our soldiers are champions

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:31.480
The blue overalls are from the battalion

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:37.240
Exactly, in this project, they are the
only ones from our construction division
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:48.480
We are live with Major General Kamel Wazir
Staff Fighter, because this is indeed a fight

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:56.480
You can see our soldiers 
cleaning and leveling the sand 

00:19:56.480 --> 00:20:00.320
so the project looks its best on the launching day

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.320
In addition to its participation in development projects

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:07.120
the armed forces have their own commercial 
projects which compete with the private sector

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:11.440
The National Service Products Organization (NSPO)
is part of the Armed Forces

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:18.000
It includes several companies in different sectors

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:23.360
industry, agricultural, poultry and livestock production,
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:32.640
contracting and construction, 
mining, general and specialized services

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:42.480
NSPO includes gas stations, general and veterinary services
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:47.040
Officers and soldiers serve there

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:54.160
They are assigned to serve at gas stations, water kiosks

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:58.840
they are assigned to provide general services. 
they sell, they buy and so on

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:00.320
These are their assignments

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:04.000
I was assigned to a farm with my battalion

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:11.520
When you are a soldier assigned to a farm, 
you are like a worker who does not get paid

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:12.960
You work for free

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:17.240
You water the trees, uproot weeds, harvest

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:22.800
work as a porter from dawn till dusk

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:30.120
Usual workers will get paid for that. 
But soldiers will not

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:38.480
Plus, you cannot exploit 
workers the way you exploit soldiers

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:52.440
Any officer who goes to a military club or 
hotel can see how all staff members are soldiers
An Officer

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:57.480
Starting from the porter to the 
receptionist, including hotel restaurant staff

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:59.680
They are all soldiers 

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:09.680
I served in the field of pastries

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:17.880
I learned how to cut a cake 
and how to prepare caramel pudding

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.000
this is a military task, isn’t it? 

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.640
A brigadier general managed the place 

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:26.880
A soldier’s salary is 230 or 235 Egyptian pound

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:31.280
The Army Command assigned a soldier to serve here

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:37.840
while Egyptian men could have been working 
in this hotel for 2.000 Egyptian pounds

00:22:37.840 --> 00:22:42.600
Why should I hire someone for 2.000 pounds 
while I can have a soldier for 200? 

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:48.800
In a gas station, instead of hiring 
someone for 1.500 pounds a month, get a soldier

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:52.480
When soldiers serve in their 
units, they get 200 pounds

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:54.680
and if they serve at the 
station they get the same amount

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:57.880
Why would I hire someone for 
1.500 when I can get a soldier?

00:22:59.160 --> 00:23:02.080
The Armed Forces' commercial projects are non-taxable

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:05.080
and no civilian party can have 
a financial monitoring over them 

00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:06.800
Leave the army alone
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:11.000
it is going well. It is a strong institution 

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.000
Why, sir? Why would we not monitor it? 

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:17.200
The People’s Assembly has a National Security Committee 

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:20.520
to oversee and monitor the Army’s budget

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:23.560
I will be very honest… 

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:30.520
Your silence holds many words

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:33.280
Or he could be thinking

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:44.280
The Army, Mr Ibrahim, is a great institution 
beyond any Egyptian’s imagination capacity  

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:50.480
When I joined the battalion, we stood in line

00:23:50.480 --> 00:23:53.040
we were asked if anyone wanted 
to go to the Commander’s office 

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:56.520
I said I did 

00:23:56.520 --> 00:23:58.160
- Come with me, soldier 

00:23:58.160 --> 00:24:01.760
Mop the floor… wash
my clothes… sweep the floor

00:24:01.760 --> 00:24:06.000
get the food ready… prepare a soup… 
get me some tea… get me coffee

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:09.120
I became a maid… 
in the army it is called "Sika" 

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:13.520
A sika is an officer’s personal assistant

00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:16.800
They serve the officer directly

00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:21.200
they are always at the officer’s 
door serving him whatever he wants

00:24:21.200 --> 00:24:24.800
If an officer lives nearby, 
a sika would run his errands

00:24:24.800 --> 00:24:28.040
He might go to buy him some 
personal stuff for the house as well 

00:24:28.040 --> 00:24:36.800
We saw a sika once polishing 
the boots of the battalion commander

00:24:36.800 --> 00:24:39.920
Well I do not stand in line

00:24:39.920 --> 00:24:44.680
I do not feel the sun’s heat. 
This is what kept me going

00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:47.120
But deep down, I never wanted to be that man 

00:24:47.120 --> 00:24:50.640
A sika soldier is feared 
by his colleagues… why? 

00:24:50.640 --> 00:24:56.800
Because he is not only a sika, 
he is also a little bird

00:24:56.800 --> 00:25:02.200
he sits with his colleagues, listens to them

00:25:02.200 --> 00:25:04.720
and reports back to the officer

00:25:04.720 --> 00:25:08.040
This impression is mostly untrue

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:15.000
It depends on the officer and his assistant

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:19.440
Sometimes the assisting soldier could 
serve his colleagues in the battalion

00:25:19.440 --> 00:25:22.480
If a soldier needs something, 
the assistant could talk to the officer about it

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:27.360
or if someone is in trouble, he 
can talk to the officer to let it go 

00:25:27.720 --> 00:25:30.040
If you do the math, for example 

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:34.720
me and two other officers had 3 sikas

00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:37.080
The Battalion Commander had 2

00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:39.480
The Head of Operations also had 2

00:25:39.480 --> 00:25:48.520
These are 7 soldiers in a battalion serving the 
officers, Battalion Commander and Head of Operations

00:25:48.520 --> 00:25:54.920
In a Brigade, the Brigadier had 6 sikas at his service 

00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:59.320
One cook, one hairdresser, one to clean and a secretary

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:05.360
If you do the math, for an entire 
year in all the brigades in the army

00:26:05.360 --> 00:26:09.240
how many sikas can you count

00:26:09.240 --> 00:26:10.920
He joined the army and completed his service...
what did you do?

00:26:10.920 --> 00:26:16.680
I cooked for the officer… I did the officer’s 
laundry… I folded the officer’s clothes

00:26:16.680 --> 00:26:18.040
that is all he did in the army 

00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:53.960
Hey Abdelwadod 

00:26:53.960 --> 00:26:57.440
you at the border

00:26:57.440 --> 00:27:01.040
you order keeper

00:27:01.040 --> 00:27:04.600
how are you? 

00:27:04.600 --> 00:27:07.800
I hope you are well

00:27:07.800 --> 00:27:11.040
keep guarding

00:27:11.040 --> 00:27:14.560
your mother pray for you

00:27:14.560 --> 00:27:17.640
she sends her regards

00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:21.120
and she tells you

00:27:21.120 --> 00:27:24.720
stay strong as your father

00:27:24.720 --> 00:27:28.080
or else they will look down on you

00:27:28.080 --> 00:27:31.800
and laugh at you

00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:41.920
I tell the Egyptian people
they could see this everyday

00:27:41.920 --> 00:27:46.200
and I brought you here to 
witness how ready our forces are

00:27:46.200 --> 00:27:50.840
and how efficient the unit
to be inspected today is

00:27:50.840 --> 00:27:53.240
They enjoy a technical 
and a fighting efficiency

00:27:53.240 --> 00:27:55.840
Technical efficiency in terms 
of weapons and vehicles

00:27:55.840 --> 00:28:00.120
and fighting efficiency in terms of 
individuals serving in their specialties 

00:28:00.840 --> 00:28:04.840
When there is an inspection visit 
to the brigade or the battalion

00:28:04.840 --> 00:28:11.400
We start training them. We train them 
how to use weapons and ammunition

00:28:11.400 --> 00:28:14.560
so before an inspection visit, it gets busy 

00:28:14.560 --> 00:28:18.360
There is something in the army 
we call "The shot", how it looks

00:28:19.640 --> 00:28:24.560
It is not important to have 
your gear secure and working

00:28:24.560 --> 00:28:29.200
it is more important you make it
look good and well-polished

00:28:29.200 --> 00:28:33.720
We would paint our gear about 20 times a year

00:28:33.720 --> 00:28:37.040
We had a dedicated unit commander

00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:41.760
To impress the Committee of the Ministry of Defense

00:28:41.760 --> 00:28:48.320
there were about 500 meters of asphalt separating 
the gate from the unit command building

00:28:48.320 --> 00:28:50.520
He decided to paint them

00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:58.000
He brought the soldiers and we 
spent 48 hours painting the asphalt

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:03.520
Colonel General Sodki Sobhi, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces, 
Minister of Defense and Military Production

00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:11.640
witnessed the practical demonstration of live 
tank shooting by the Armed Forces Artillery Unit

00:29:11.640 --> 00:29:18.400
This goes in line with the yearly military training 
plan of the Armed Forces divisions and units 

00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:25.240
Soldiers who attend war simulations
benefit a lot from the army 

00:29:25.240 --> 00:29:26.760
They are highly trained for combat

00:29:26.760 --> 00:29:29.480
But those who are not trained for war 
do not receive the same combat training

00:29:29.480 --> 00:29:32.280
The best they receive is the shooting training

00:29:32.280 --> 00:29:37.880
Do you know how many months a soldier 
has to spend practicing for this show? 

00:29:37.880 --> 00:29:39.480
He spends 3 or 4 months

00:29:40.720 --> 00:29:44.760
in a desert, being insulted and tortured

00:29:44.760 --> 00:29:48.440
to have those 5 minutes before the 
Marshal or the Minister of Defense

00:29:48.440 --> 00:29:51.720
or before the Commander 
who will come and supervise

00:29:51.720 --> 00:29:54.200
The "shot" is everything 

00:29:54.200 --> 00:29:57.840
Thanks to God, we have a strong Artillery

00:29:57.840 --> 00:30:05.600
It is very accurate and able to 
perform in a high professional way

00:30:06.440 --> 00:30:11.960
The equipment we are trained 
to use are called training equipment

00:30:11.960 --> 00:30:14.440
They are very old

00:30:14.440 --> 00:30:22.000
The equipment we are trained to use and train 
our soldiers to use goes back to the 1973 war.

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.400
I was a tank aimer

00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:28.200
I used to sit in a tank, aim and fire

00:30:28.200 --> 00:30:30.240
I handled a T62 tank

00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:34.600
I guess it is now a piece in 
the Russian military heritage

00:30:34.600 --> 00:30:40.040
I aimed and fired

00:30:40.520 --> 00:30:43.120
It fell 200 meters away from the target

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:47.920
I fixed the barrel and fired again

00:30:47.920 --> 00:30:53.760
It fell 200 meters away, in the same spot

00:30:54.480 --> 00:30:59.520
I gave it a thought and calculated the distance

00:30:59.520 --> 00:31:02.960
moved the barrel 100 meters away from the target
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:31:02.960 --> 00:31:04.720
When I fired, it hit the target!

00:31:05.480 --> 00:31:07.960
The Weapons Director was visiting once

00:31:07.960 --> 00:31:09.520
When I asked him

00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:13.760
he said of course they had Sophisticated weapons 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:31:13.760 --> 00:31:16.800
and officers were being 
trained elsewhere to use them

00:31:16.800 --> 00:31:21.040
Sophisticated weapons, haven’t 
you heard of weapon dealsl?

00:31:21.040 --> 00:31:27.480
But we cannot use those weapons 
to train soldiers. They will ruin them

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:29.640
If you have sophisticated weapons

00:31:29.640 --> 00:31:33.240
and you are training trusted officers 
and paying them to handle them

00:31:33.240 --> 00:31:36.760
why am I was forced to join the 
army to train on useless weapons?

00:31:36.760 --> 00:31:38.920
You brought me here for nothing 

00:32:23.440 --> 00:32:31.680
The fighting capacity is 
the result of two main factors

00:32:31.680 --> 00:32:34.080
the individual and the equipment

00:32:34.080 --> 00:32:41.240
Qualified individuals, highly trained for combat

00:32:41.240 --> 00:32:45.880
and sophisticated technical equipment

00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:54.520
convenient to the soldiers’ capacity, 
the battlefield and the nature of the fight

00:32:55.800 --> 00:32:58.320
The next day, we were serving

00:32:58.320 --> 00:33:00.760
we were assigned to the fortifications

00:33:00.760 --> 00:33:03.000
mosquitos were as big as buffalos

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:05.400
ripping through our overalls

00:33:05.400 --> 00:33:07.920
hours went by like years

00:33:07.920 --> 00:33:10.480
sikas were not loyal

00:33:10.480 --> 00:33:12.960
breakfast is served at 6 am

00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:15.440
are those beans or rot?

00:33:15.440 --> 00:33:17.760
Of course, you suffer from indigestion

00:33:17.760 --> 00:33:20.360
but who will care about us?

00:33:22.840 --> 00:33:25.200
The officers’ food was 
incomparable with the soldiers’

00:33:26.320 --> 00:33:31.160
Soldiers’ food was worse than bad

00:33:31.160 --> 00:33:33.920
You are stuck with what you 
have whether you like it or not 

00:33:33.920 --> 00:33:36.160
As for officers’ food, it was something else

00:33:36.160 --> 00:33:38.760
They had their meals in 
a neat and clean place

00:33:39.440 --> 00:33:42.920
Some soldiers would get 
their revenge from officers 

00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:47.240
by spitting in their food as they cook it

00:33:47.240 --> 00:33:50.440
Every now and then, a commander 
comes and sits with us

00:33:50.440 --> 00:33:51.640
He asks if we have any complaints

00:33:51.640 --> 00:33:56.840
We usually complained about 
the bad food and the small quantities

00:33:56.840 --> 00:34:00.800
He would say: in every brigade, 
there are 3 thousand soldiers

00:34:00.800 --> 00:34:03.800
If we spend 1 pound per 
soldier on food every day

00:34:03.800 --> 00:34:06.560
we would be spending 
3.000 pounds a day on one brigade

00:34:06.560 --> 00:34:08.880
and 100.000 pounds a month

00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:12.920
How many brigades and soldiers do we have? 

00:34:12.920 --> 00:34:16.760
and our country’s economy is weak; 
how should we buy all this food? 

00:34:16.760 --> 00:34:18.960
That is what he would say

00:34:18.960 --> 00:34:22.160
then why bring me to the army in the first place? 

00:34:22.760 --> 00:34:32.080
Do they do it on purpose to teach soldiers 
to eat everything and not to complain about food?

00:34:32.080 --> 00:34:32.880
I do not know

00:34:32.880 --> 00:34:35.280
If you want me to get 
used to eating anything

00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:38.120
you should do that in times of training

00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:41.160
when we are in a certain psychological state
when we feel we are warriors 

00:34:41.160 --> 00:34:46.000
and not prisoners whom you 
feed anything so they do not object

00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.480
If soldiers should eat anything, 

00:34:49.480 --> 00:34:51.880
why is this not the case for officers? 

00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:54.480
Will they not be together in the battlefield?

00:35:12.240 --> 00:35:17.040
We were assigned on duty
that is when we are required to serve

00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:21.080
A number of soldiers from 
our battalion were assigned

00:35:21.080 --> 00:35:28.920
The NCO told the officer who wanted us to 
go on duty and who was from another battalion

00:35:28.920 --> 00:35:34.400
that it was lunch hour and if it was 
possible we have lunch before we go

00:35:34.400 --> 00:35:35.520
The officer said they 
needed us right away

00:35:35.520 --> 00:35:41.560
We were shocked when we realized we 
were going to clean the officers’ residence

00:35:41.560 --> 00:35:44.720
It was lunch hour, and 
the officers were eating

00:35:44.720 --> 00:35:50.280
We stood there. They were sitting in 
their five-star food court having lunch 

00:35:50.280 --> 00:35:55.680
as we stared at them، hungry, 
waiting to clean after them

00:35:55.680 --> 00:35:57.960
One officer was outside. 
He was not eating

00:35:57.960 --> 00:36:04.160
He saw the soldiers standing 
and staring as the officers ate

00:36:04.160 --> 00:36:06.840
He screamed: turn!

00:36:06.840 --> 00:36:09.040
We did

00:36:09.040 --> 00:36:14.760
and by that we turned our 
backs to the officers’ food court

00:36:14.760 --> 00:36:17.240
so we do not see the officers eating

00:36:17.240 --> 00:36:22.320
while we were brought 
hungry to clean after them

00:36:22.320 --> 00:36:26.800
It was very humiliating

00:36:26.800 --> 00:36:31.160
My whole life, I have 
never felt as humiliated

00:36:37.720 --> 00:36:45.840
In the army, there are officers,
non-commissioned officers 

00:36:45.840 --> 00:36:47.400
and soldiers

00:36:51.200 --> 00:36:55.920
An officer only addresses soldiers 
through non-commissioned officers 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:36:55.920 --> 00:37:01.200
A non-commissioned officer is 
usually a preparatory school graduate 

00:37:01.200 --> 00:37:02.640
and an army volunteer

00:37:02.640 --> 00:37:04.840
There is a saying in the army

00:37:04.840 --> 00:37:08.040
when you say “I was thinking”, 
they ask you: “thinking?”

00:37:08.040 --> 00:37:10.280
Rest your brain

00:37:10.280 --> 00:37:13.280
It is common among non-commissioned officers

00:37:13.280 --> 00:37:16.200
They are the trainers

00:37:16.200 --> 00:37:19.760
They feel they are the 
most maltreated in the army

00:37:19.760 --> 00:37:24.520
They are not well respected officers

00:37:24.920 --> 00:37:27.560
and they are not soldiers 
who serve a year and leave

00:37:27.560 --> 00:37:29.640
They feel they are wronged

00:37:29.640 --> 00:37:32.200
Officers mistreat them and 
humiliate them in front of soldiers 

00:37:32.200 --> 00:37:34.840
and soldiers stand up to them 

00:37:35.240 --> 00:37:42.240
Non-commissioned officers are the main pillar 
which promotes performance in units and formations

00:37:42.240 --> 00:37:46.040
Their slogan is: belief, determination, sacrifice

00:37:47.200 --> 00:37:49.240
Of course I am staying all my life in the army

00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:52.840
I will not be treated like 
an officer, and this is unjust

00:37:52.840 --> 00:37:55.200
but what can I do? 
This is my job
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:37:55.200 --> 00:37:57.600
Even people with normal work are fed up

00:37:57.600 --> 00:38:00.760
I swear I was a good 
student, and I studied well

00:38:00.760 --> 00:38:07.360
but I was fed up with 
school and dropped out

00:38:07.360 --> 00:38:09.000
But this is my job, what can I do? 

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:34.080
The relationship of soldiers with 
non-commissioned officers is always very bad

00:38:34.080 --> 00:38:38.400
They mistreat soldiers, 
punish and abuse them

00:38:38.400 --> 00:38:42.000
No, we do not torture them

00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:44.280
We only punished them when we felt like it

00:38:44.280 --> 00:38:48.360
I remember I woke the soldiers up 
once at 2 in the morning

00:38:48.360 --> 00:38:50.800
It was freezing

00:38:50.800 --> 00:38:53.600
I made them stand in line

00:38:53.600 --> 00:38:56.160
I ordered them to take their clothes off

00:38:56.160 --> 00:38:57.800
They did

00:38:57.800 --> 00:39:01.720
You know how difficult it is 
to stay naked in the cold

00:39:01.720 --> 00:39:06.600
I ordered them to lie down 
and sprayed them with water

00:39:06.600 --> 00:39:10.640
I made them crawl in the field 

00:39:10.640 --> 00:39:13.120
For some non-commissioned officers

00:39:13.120 --> 00:39:20.240
you can be a university graduate, but they 
will always want to prove you are weak 

00:39:20.240 --> 00:39:26.040
We beat them, mistreat them
until they learn to obey

00:39:26.040 --> 00:39:35.960
especially those university graduates 
who think they are far better than us

00:39:35.960 --> 00:39:39.120
when actually they work as sikas and in offices

00:39:39.120 --> 00:39:41.640
They are not qualified for the tough military life

00:39:55.520 --> 00:39:58.400
I knew a non-commissioned officer 
who would always say:

00:39:58.400 --> 00:40:00.280
Do not ever think you are smarter than me

00:40:00.280 --> 00:40:01.920
because I am smarter than you

00:40:01.920 --> 00:40:02.920
For no reason

00:40:02.920 --> 00:40:06.560
No one tried to prove they were smarter than him

00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:08.720
He just liked to repeat that

00:40:09.240 --> 00:40:11.200
It reassured him

00:40:12.520 --> 00:40:15.200
In the army, it is a matter of seniority

00:40:15.200 --> 00:40:18.480
Any senior has the 
right to give you orders

00:40:18.480 --> 00:40:20.040
There are two types of seniors

00:40:20.040 --> 00:40:22.040
those who joined before you, 
and those with a higher rank

00:40:22.040 --> 00:40:24.080
You sense fear everywhere

00:40:24.080 --> 00:40:27.120
Soldiers fear NCOs and officers

00:40:27.120 --> 00:40:29.320
NCOs fear officers

00:40:29.320 --> 00:40:31.320
The army was established on fear 

00:40:31.320 --> 00:40:33.000
Where does this chain end? 

00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:36.800
When you can no longer mistreat 
your junior because you have none

00:40:36.800 --> 00:40:38.360
Soldiers are at the end of the chain

00:40:38.360 --> 00:40:43.880
They are subject to all forms of oppression 
and stress going through the chain

00:40:43.880 --> 00:40:46.000
They absorb them and keep them in 

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:48.240
A soldier is like a rubber band

00:40:48.240 --> 00:40:51.280
the more pressure you put on it, 
the more you control it

00:40:51.280 --> 00:40:52.640
Once you let go, it 
bounces back at you 

00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:57.600
Soldiers will not learn 
discipline without punishment

00:40:57.600 --> 00:40:59.360
Punishment comes in stages

00:40:59.360 --> 00:41:02.200
The worst you can do is deprive 
a soldier from going on holiday

00:41:02.200 --> 00:41:04.360
or refer him to the military court

00:41:04.360 --> 00:41:06.640
You can also punish a soldier in the field

00:41:06.640 --> 00:41:08.400
make them take the 6th position

00:41:08.400 --> 00:41:11.680
The 6th position is the push-up position

00:41:11.680 --> 00:41:15.400
You lie down on your stomach 
and you crawl for half an hour 
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:41:15.400 --> 00:41:16.800
There is something they call the grill

00:41:16.800 --> 00:41:23.720
You lie down and roll on 
the asphalt under the sun

00:41:24.680 --> 00:41:28.400
Suffering is not necessarily humiliating

00:41:29.640 --> 00:41:34.080
When you are forced to walk for 20 kilometers

00:41:34.080 --> 00:41:37.600
you suffer but you become a man

00:41:37.600 --> 00:41:44.920
But if when I am walking I say I am 
tired and you hit me and curse me

00:41:44.920 --> 00:41:47.920
you might think it will make me a man

00:41:47.920 --> 00:41:50.200
but in that way you broke me

00:41:50.200 --> 00:41:53.120
Obey, then object

00:41:53.120 --> 00:41:55.880
If you believe you have been wronged

00:41:55.880 --> 00:41:59.400
do as you are told then complain 
to a higher ranking officer

00:41:59.400 --> 00:42:04.520
For instance, if you see a 
shaver thrown in the bathroom 

00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:06.800
and he orders you to shave with it

00:42:06.800 --> 00:42:08.840
you shave and then you complain

00:42:08.840 --> 00:42:14.520
If you file a complaint at the military 
investigators or the Ministry of Defense 

00:42:14.520 --> 00:42:16.160
and it went unheeded,

00:42:16.160 --> 00:42:18.480
can you imagine what will happen to you?

00:42:18.480 --> 00:42:19.880
In the army, we go by two rules: 

00:42:19.880 --> 00:42:24.640
No cursing, but I can insult you, 
and no beating

00:42:24.640 --> 00:42:31.920
Insults are known, such as filthy, nasty, ugly

00:42:32.520 --> 00:42:34.000
but no one is allowed to curse you

00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:36.240
But if you join the army 
and live there for a while, 

00:42:36.240 --> 00:42:38.680
you realize you are always cursed

00:42:38.680 --> 00:42:39.760
You have no right to object 

00:42:39.840 --> 00:42:49.800
New soldiers need to be cursed to be disciplined

00:42:49.800 --> 00:42:52.360
In the army, someone cursed my mother

00:42:52.360 --> 00:42:54.120
I had never experienced this

00:42:54.120 --> 00:42:56.040
He said: you son of a…

00:42:56.720 --> 00:42:57.920
it really hurt

00:42:58.520 --> 00:43:03.720
I looked at him and he said: 
do you have something to say you son of…

00:43:03.720 --> 00:43:06.320
He was a brigadier general and I was a soldier

00:43:06.320 --> 00:43:08.080
I knew what that meant

00:43:08.080 --> 00:43:11.240
I saw with my own eyes, when a brigadier general 
wants to address a lieutenant

00:43:11.240 --> 00:43:13.880
he orders the colonel to do it

00:43:13.880 --> 00:43:15.880
because he does not stoop down 
to the level of a lieutenant

00:43:15.880 --> 00:43:17.160
let alone a soldier

00:43:17.160 --> 00:43:18.480
A soldier is no officer

00:43:18.480 --> 00:43:24.080
A soldier for a general 
is like an ant for a dinosaur

00:43:24.080 --> 00:43:26.320
If a dinosaur steps on 
an elephant, it will crush it

00:43:26.320 --> 00:43:29.840
An elephant will crush a deer

00:43:29.840 --> 00:43:32.440
An ant is crushed by all

00:43:32.440 --> 00:43:35.280
In the forest, all animals 
crush ants as they move 

00:43:35.280 --> 00:43:41.840
The colonel gathered us and said: 

00:43:41.840 --> 00:43:46.120
when I curse you, do not be mad. Why? 
For a very simple reason

00:43:46.120 --> 00:43:49.560
When I get mad at you, 
I have two options

00:43:49.680 --> 00:43:52.840
I can either ruin your 
dossier and punish you

00:43:52.840 --> 00:43:55.840
or I can let the anger 
out by cursing you

00:43:55.840 --> 00:44:00.840
When you join the unit, I want you 
to check your dignity at the door 

00:44:00.840 --> 00:44:08.680
When you join the army you realize 
you can easily get beaten by an officer

00:44:08.680 --> 00:44:10.040
and try to complain if you can

00:44:10.040 --> 00:44:12.600
You do not realize what full power means

00:44:12.600 --> 00:44:20.400
having 30-soldier unit in a desert controlled 
by one officer who can do whatever he likes

00:44:20.400 --> 00:44:22.400
no limits

00:44:22.400 --> 00:44:26.920
One time, an officer hung a soldier by his 
feet and ordered other soldiers to pull him

00:44:26.920 --> 00:44:28.880
How insulting!

00:44:28.880 --> 00:44:34.400
We heard screams coming from 
the officer’s office: gather everyone

00:44:34.400 --> 00:44:36.160
The unit had to gather and so we did

00:44:36.160 --> 00:44:40.640
We had to take our clothes off and stand in line

00:44:40.640 --> 00:44:42.320
Why?

00:44:42.320 --> 00:44:44.680
Because Al Ahli team lost the championship
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:44:44.680 --> 00:44:47.880
The Chief of Operations supported Al Ahli
He was a big fan

00:44:47.880 --> 00:44:51.680
Then he punished us when they tied
How great! Getting punished for Al Ahli

00:44:52.240 --> 00:45:00.120
The worst punishing tactic for an officer or an NCO 
is to prohibit a soldier from taking a day off

00:45:00.120 --> 00:45:06.840
This is the worst punishing 
method that destroys a soldier 

00:45:06.840 --> 00:45:10.400
Some soldiers would spend 
3 months with no day off

00:45:10.400 --> 00:45:13.120
so they would do something very strange

00:45:13.120 --> 00:45:16.520
A soldier would tie a bandage around his knee

00:45:16.520 --> 00:45:18.280
we call it a tourniquet

00:45:18.280 --> 00:45:21.240
to stop the blood flow

00:45:21.240 --> 00:45:22.480
then go to sleep

00:45:22.480 --> 00:45:25.280
He would wake up with 
his leg feeling numb

00:45:25.280 --> 00:45:30.800
He would then take something 
hard and break his leg with it

00:45:33.680 --> 00:45:33.720
Once he breaks it, 
he would untie the tourniquet 

00:45:33.720 --> 00:45:39.600
so the blood flows back to his leg
He would feel unbearable pain

00:45:40.600 --> 00:45:41.600
He broke his leg

00:45:41.600 --> 00:45:44.400
You cannot forbid him from 
taking a month and a half off

00:45:44.400 --> 00:45:50.680
You can only imagine how they live 
and what they feel when in the battalion 

00:45:51.240 --> 00:45:53.000
Yes, some soldiers ran away

00:45:53.000 --> 00:45:55.680
They went on holiday 
and never came back 

00:45:55.680 --> 00:46:00.680
A soldier ran away because 
an officer hung him by his foot

00:46:00.680 --> 00:46:03.160
He left and never came back

00:46:03.160 --> 00:46:08.720
You join the army with the belief that 
it is the worst thing that will happen to you

00:46:08.720 --> 00:46:12.080
but you have to go through it 
to move on with your life

00:46:12.080 --> 00:46:15.040
Of course, some do not 
move on with their lives

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:19.800
They commit suicide in the army 

00:46:21.360 --> 00:46:23.400
A soldier was not given a leave

00:46:23.400 --> 00:46:25.920
His mother was dying 
and he wanted to see her

00:46:25.920 --> 00:46:28.520
The officer did not want to 
give him permission to leave

00:46:28.520 --> 00:46:31.200
He told him: I will not give you permission, 
I do not feel like it

00:46:31.200 --> 00:46:36.320
The soldier begged him, please, let me go

00:46:36.320 --> 00:46:40.960
He decided to come up 
with a plan to escape

00:46:40.960 --> 00:46:43.040
He was caught

00:46:43.040 --> 00:46:45.840
The officer told him: even if your mother dies, 
I will not let you go

00:46:45.840 --> 00:46:47.440
His mother passed away while 
he was still in the army

00:46:47.440 --> 00:46:51.520
He got too mad that he shot the officer

00:46:51.520 --> 00:46:53.240
he shot him in his room

00:46:53.240 --> 00:46:55.240
here

00:46:56.200 --> 00:47:02.840
I remember there was a soldier serving 
in the Republican Guard

00:47:02.840 --> 00:47:05.240
He got fed up with all the orders and punishing

00:47:05.240 --> 00:47:07.800
so he shot the officer and the NCO

00:47:07.800 --> 00:47:09.880
Then he shot himself

00:47:09.880 --> 00:47:12.080
He committed suicide 

00:47:12.080 --> 00:47:18.040
I used to read the faxes we received because 
I handled operations, organization and management

00:47:19.400 --> 00:47:25.160
We mostly received faxes about 
soldiers committing suicide

00:47:25.160 --> 00:47:26.760
The official reason?

00:47:27.120 --> 00:47:32.840
Unheeded instructions and orders stressing 
the need for raising religious awareness among soldiers

00:47:32.840 --> 00:47:35.160
This is not the real reason

00:47:35.160 --> 00:47:37.400
Why would a soldier commit suicide?

00:47:37.400 --> 00:47:39.640
Because you are not providing 
enough religious education? 

00:47:39.640 --> 00:47:45.440
No, you are bringing a Sheikh to preach 
every Thursday that suicide is Haram

00:47:45.440 --> 00:47:50.800
But when the Sheikh leaves, 
officers torture and torment soldiers

00:47:50.800 --> 00:47:52.720
This leads the soldiers to suicide

00:47:52.720 --> 00:47:56.760
Fine, suicide is Haram, but 
what about what you are doing? ? Is it not Haram? 

00:47:56.760 --> 00:48:00.640
All this humiliation, and only suicide is haram?  

00:48:02.320 --> 00:48:09.600
We believed the army was our spirit breaker

00:48:09.600 --> 00:48:13.040
That expression was common 

00:48:13.040 --> 00:48:16.120
The hardest thing in life is 
to have someone control you

00:48:17.840 --> 00:48:20.880
Soldiers are the most inferior in the army

00:48:23.160 --> 00:48:28.400
I asked an officer once 
why we were humiliated all the time

00:48:28.400 --> 00:48:32.320
He told me they were training us 
on harsh conditions in capture

00:48:32.320 --> 00:48:35.840
I said: why don’t you teach us how to fight first,
before you teach us how to behave when captured?

00:48:35.840 --> 00:48:37.400
Why do you do it the other way around?

00:48:37.400 --> 00:48:41.360
Train me to fight. 
I might not be captured  and succeed 

00:49:17.320 --> 00:49:21.720
The day before we left the army,
before our last day in the unit

00:49:21.720 --> 00:49:25.560
we partied so hard.
We spent our day dancing

00:49:25.560 --> 00:49:36.720
Dancing and partying was as close as we felt 
to the real world and to other people

00:49:36.720 --> 00:49:41.600
Within the army, 
we build strong friendships

00:49:41.600 --> 00:49:43.480
We undergo the same torturing

00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:47.640
We stand together because we are all miserable 

00:49:52.160 --> 00:49:55.120
I served my time and did not learn anything new

00:49:55.120 --> 00:49:58.480
I even lost a few things

00:49:58.480 --> 00:50:01.160
I suffered from severe psychological issues 

00:50:01.160 --> 00:50:04.480
Joining the army taught me a lot

00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:08.320
I met different people
both good and bad

00:50:08.320 --> 00:50:16.200
liars… hypocrites… people who wanted 
to manipulate others at any cost… 

00:50:16.200 --> 00:50:19.840
I have nothing to do with wars,
I know nothing about them

00:50:19.840 --> 00:50:22.840
I used to plant and harvest

00:50:22.840 --> 00:50:26.600
I have nothing to do with wars

00:50:26.600 --> 00:50:30.240
You can find other responsible people in wars...
but not me!

00:50:30.240 --> 00:50:33.160
When war erupts, we will die

00:50:33.160 --> 00:50:34.720
and others will fight

00:50:34.720 --> 00:50:36.080
who are those others and 
what will they fight with?

00:50:36.080 --> 00:50:37.440
My guess is as good as yours

00:50:37.440 --> 00:50:39.080
There’s a common belief in the army

00:50:39.080 --> 00:50:41.920
if war erupts, there is another army that will fight

00:50:41.920 --> 00:50:45.400
I do not know how to use a weapon 
and I have never been trained on tactics

00:50:45.400 --> 00:50:49.480
The rifle I was trained to use was made in 1954

00:50:49.480 --> 00:50:53.440
I was trained on a 50-year-old rifle 

00:50:53.440 --> 00:50:55.280
What war are you talking about?!

00:50:55.560 --> 00:51:01.600
30 soldiers were killed after two separate 
attacks on army points in Northern Sinai

00:51:01.600 --> 00:51:10.840
After the death of 27 soldiers in a terrorist attack 
that targeted tanks in Karm Alkawadis, south Areish

00:51:10.840 --> 00:51:15.080
our reporter informed us that at least 3 others were 
killed as a result of an attack on an army checkpoint 

00:51:15.200 --> 00:51:23.200
Many Egyptian soldiers, NCO and officers were killed by a series 
of attacksbetween June 2013 and the screening of the movie

00:51:24.120 --> 00:51:26.560
A Film by
Emadeldin Elsayed

00:51:27.520 --> 00:51:30.320
Producer
Ahmed Elmasry

00:51:47.520 --> 00:51:53.360
Special thanks to all who took part in making this movie 
and whose names were not mentioned for safety reasons

